SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Single Assessment Timing Requirements Reminder
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Single Assessment Timing Requirements Reminder\nSingle 
 Assessment Timing Requirements Reminder\nAug 11\, 2026\nT\nhe summary belo
 w outlines the timing requirements for initial and repeat Single Assessmen
 ts\, including the limited exceptions to the standard annual assessment cy
 cle for children receiving medium- and high-intensity behavioral health se
 rvices.\nSituation\nWhen is a Single Assessment Required?\nTiming\nChild a
 lready receiving services (no prior Single Assessment)\nIf the child has n
 ever had a Single Assessment\, complete one before the next authorization 
 is issued. After that\, follow the standard annual reassessment schedule.\
 nBefore the next authorization (typically at the next Continued Stay Revie
 w (CSR))\, then every\n12\nmonths\nNew request for medium- or high-intensi
 ty services\nComplete a Single Assessment before submitting the initial re
 ferral or authorization request.\nInitial assessment\nChild continues rece
 iving medium- or high-intensity services\nRepeat the Single Assessment to 
 confirm ongoing eligibility. Continue submitting CSRs between annual asses
 sments.\nEvery 12 months\nChild residing in a Children’s Residential Car
 e Facility (CRCF)\nComplete a Single Assessment when discharge planning be
 gins to determine eligibility for community-based services after discharge
 .\nAt discharge planning\nOn a CRCF wait list\nRepeat the Single Assessmen
 t while the child remains on the wait list.\nEvery 6 months\nChild receivi
 ng services that began before the Single Assessment process was implemente
 d\nIf no Single Assessment has been completed and the current authorizatio
 n is nearing expiration\, complete an initial Single Assessment before the
  next authorization. After that\, follow the annual reassessment schedule.
 \nAt the first CSR after Single Assessment implementation\, then every 12 
 months thereafter.\nFor questions\, please contact\nKaren Sax-McLoughlin\,
 \nP\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/single-as
 sessment-timing-requirements-reminder-2026-08-11
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/single-ass
 essment-timing-requirements-reminder-2026-08-11
